{
  "_about": "Model term -> role and layout column. Terms come from analysis.model in study_spec.json (Biodes design_catalog.json; since Biodes 6e49dab the catalog uses generic terms: treatment treatment2 block rep row col unit subject time env period sequence check). Column lookup order: analysis.terms.columns[term] if Biodes gives it; the term itself when it is listed in analysis.terms.layout_columns; the n-th spec factor name (from_spec_factor); columns, in order; the term's own name. A column whose every value joins several factors with combined_level_separator (a cell label such as 'dry:H4') is skipped when the model has two or more fixed treatment terms. role: treatment (effects of interest), block (nuisance: drawn at random, fitted as written), unit (experimental unit or subject: grouping only). Old term names (genotype, main, sub, A, B, ...) stay for packages written before the generic terms.",
